                <pb facs="0244" n="232" sameAs="frus:frus1943v02/pg232"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851B.24/78: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Consul General in
                        Martinique</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Malige</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-02-27T17:00:00-04:00">February 27,
                            1943—5 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>47. Your 86, February 25. We assume that Admiral Robert has intentionally
                    distorted the facts in order to obtain the ends he desires from Vichy. As you
                    are aware, however, we have not yet gone beyond telling him that withdrawal of
                    the gentlemen’s agreement may be necessary. For your information, this may have
                    to be done in the near future. As you are also aware, we have at no time
                    expressed a desire to conclude “another agreement”.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berle</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
